WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.730
Nonclastic sediment can form from dissolved components instead of fragments broken

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.830
from older rock. As salty lake or sea water evaporates, minerals

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.390
such as halite and gypsum can precipitate.

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:14.310
Other chemical reactions also make minerals.

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.630
Evaporation removes water; the dissolved material is left behind and becomes

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.510
concentrated before precipitation.

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:25.450
Calcium-rich spring water can deposit layered calcite as travertine.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.270
Organisms also extract dissolved chemicals to build shells and skeletons.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:33.410
Accumulated carbonate remains can become limestone.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:38.690
Chemical and biological processes may work together, so the contrast concerns

00:00:38.690 --> 00:00:42.810
the stated formation pathway rather than an absolute separation of all

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:43.690
natural examples.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:49.190
Chalk is a soft, very fine-grained limestone made from microscopic calcium-carbonate

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:54.270
remains. Dolostone can form when magnesium-bearing groundwater reacts with limestone, replacing

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:58.530
calcite with dolomite. This changes the mineral composition of an existing

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:02.230
carbonate rock; it is different from simply compacting an untouched pile

00:01:02.230 --> 00:01:03.310
of shell fragments.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:08.650
Chert is silica rich. It can form from accumulated microscopic silica

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:13.210
shells or from chemical precipitation, including nodules in carbonate rock.

00:01:13.370 --> 00:01:17.510
Iron formation contains thin layers rich in iron minerals, commonly with

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:19.970
quartz, and much of it formed early in Earth history.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.950
Similar layering therefore does not mean identical composition or origin.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:28.650
Wetlands can accumulate plant debris faster than it is completely destroyed.

00:01:29.190 --> 00:01:32.470
Peat retains much of the original plant texture and pore space.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:36.590
With burial, compaction and heating, peat loses water and oxygen and

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:39.850
becomes coal. Carbon-rich coal records plant material;

00:01:40.110 --> 00:01:42.590
it is not an evaporite and is not made from a

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:43.790
pile of quartz sand.
